1a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which American space shuttle broke apart while re-entering the atmosphere in 2003?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Columbia was lost after launch damage compromised its thermal protection, allowing extreme heat to destroy the orbiter during re-entry.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5546-71b3-b2bd-e05001662cc0","description":"Columbia","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7952-934d-4628af37b3ae","description":"Challenger","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7963-828b-fc33bd6f4e60","description":"Discovery","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7ca6-b169-35873492dc77","description":"Atlantis","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-71f7-ab87-18726f298182","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"On which continent do most of the world\'s wild cheetahs live?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Most wild cheetahs live in sub-Saharan Africa, with a small remnant in Iran.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7c74-bda6-0e7a0f5f7b16","description":"Africa","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7dc6-b3d8-02681915395d","description":"Australia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7f13-99ca-699b1b28a8c2","description":"Europe","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7456-b5ee-8ae6ffded1d5","description":"South America","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7449-9bce-53477b97d7d0","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What are the first digits of pi?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"3.14 is a common approximation of pi, whose decimal digits continue forever without repeating.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7c2e-a16d-94961ddfe0e4","description":"3.14","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7008-8e7e-383cdc535cc2","description":"3.41","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7ffa-a4e2-380030ac9a96","description":"4.31","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-78c3-9237-55d51db1c59d"