,{"id":"01a218eb-5546-75a3-b3e2-82ca3bf7a3cf","description":"Snails","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7b22-95dd-262f3bfe58b4","description":"Fish","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7c81-9a86-a93280dc1d4b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"The cranium, which encloses the brain, is part of which larger bony structure?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The skull includes both the cranium, which protects the brain, and the facial bones.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5546-77c8-a55a-9109f33f9ab7","description":"Skull","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7948-a41e-f401acdee955","description":"Pelvis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-729f-9c35-52604d9e88a9","description":"Spine","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-72f8-a10d-01edb93aff8e","description":"Ribcage","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-77a0-a00b-1ac6d2e3f75b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who developed the theory of evolution by natural selection?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Charles Darwin set out natural selection in On the Origin of Species (1859), developed after his voyage on HMS Beagle.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7db8-a072-2b89d7e5c04a","description":"Charles Darwin","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-74f8-8a2c-5188645fa571","description":"Albert Einstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7798-9775-7d99be9c7d00","description":"Isaac Newton","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7eae-ac5d-63ac88fabb81","description":"Galileo Galilei","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-704e-8d93-0bf3f0b80e76","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which term refers to objects or lines that are side by side and will never intersect?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Parallel lines stay the same distance apart; perpendicular lines meet at a right angle, while convergent lines move toward one another.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5546-73fb-84a1-1ec0d4cede52","description":"Parallel","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-758f-9b4a-e142793523a6","description":"Perpendicular","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7642-9b1c-3bad6973e8aa","description":"Diagonal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7b11-9880-f78a1d6b0ca8","description":"Convergent","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7641-8dbe-c93f7bfa32e4","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Marine iguanas, saltwater crocodiles, sea snakes and sea turtles all belong to which class of animals?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Reptiles are air-breathing vertebrates with scales. Sea turtles must surface for air, while marine iguanas can hold their breath underwater.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5546-726c-9dc4-565b091251c0","description":"Reptiles","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-749a-b006-3b14b18b4d7f","description":"Mammals","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7bfc-877c-5bd844ff2fd4","description":"Amphibians","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7dff-a6b9-2180969c17e6","description":"Fish","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7b29-9527-22ed855cf6b3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What would you call a baby owl?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"An owlet is a young owl; the ending -let often marks something small or young, as in piglet.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7ba3-bae5-e1ca3030c62a","description":"An Owlet","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-79be-9f43-0b82e7179cac","description":"A Caterpillar","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-748f-9af8-bc4800494bfe","description":"A Codling","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-72ea-9fbe-1ea15df91b46","description":"A Colt","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5546-7453-b53e-7d977dc96ba9","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","