rrect_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7d93-a391-e6d21d85aa76","description":"Distillation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-71bf-9c96-3273b61b2025","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the term for a mineral that contains metal?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"An ore contains enough valuable material to make extraction worthwhile; not every metal-bearing rock qualifies.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7a9d-beb9-4ff6e07fdf95","description":"Ore","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7f0b-af2a-2c2d570e823d","description":"Peat","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-745c-90c7-8b2418a9b325","description":"Stone","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7f13-bb19-040a47dab94a","description":"Cement","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-78f1-a7e3-d0dec887662d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"A female deer is known as what?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A doe is also an adult female rabbit; an adult male deer is called a buck.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-744a-9046-d2e6161bf501","description":"A Doe","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7223-a50b-ec294896b33a","description":"A Pen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7437-b8b1-b83bb540777a","description":"A Mare","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-71a2-9151-8c4b33305ef5","description":"A Nanny","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7bfd-887f-18a6b7c5f122","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What kind of organism is a leech?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A leech is a parasite because it feeds on a host; many species use suckers to attach to animals.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7f0c-bf46-d0ab68aebc38","description":"Parasite","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-70fe-9c0d-42cadea0bfe1","description":"Herbivore","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-78a5-9c89-e75aced6e098","description":"Omnivore","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7f3a-8074-350d1451cab5","description":"Decomposer","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-791d-ada2-e46d0dcd7d2f","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the largest snake?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Anacondas are generally considered the largest snakes by weight, though reticulated pythons can grow longer.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-740d-b1b9-db8c33e04f81","description":"Anaconda","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7fac-af4e-5bb4069a76d1","description":"Black mamba","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7b72-a749-b0767a63864c","description":"Rattlesnake","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-761a-b74e-e29aba925b27","description":"King cobra","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-72c2-b7c7-d0acbdf88304","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What type of shape might be obtuse or isosceles?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A triangle\'s angles total 180 degrees; obtuse describes one angle greater than 90 degrees, while isosceles means two sides are equal.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-793d-a9a7-259a2eea2d72","description":"A Triangle","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7f5b-ae55-d1ac11b9b377","description":"A Square","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7559-b18b-d0a988932480","description":"A Circle","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7791-ab2e-310d08f53678","description":"A Rectangle","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7706-a782-bab2f8fd4645","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is made out of gravel, sand, cement and water?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Concrete hardens as cement reacts with water, binding the sand and gravel together.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-791d-a84d-08633ac7f291","description":"Concrete","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7ff4-b2d1-356b7b439da1","description":"Porcelain","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7aa1-9e14-26a783a4b4ec","description":"Gypsum","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7255-8350-cc185355ac81","description":"Chalk","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7e2a-b41e-287bbef6c418","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many limbs does an octopus have?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"An octopus has 8 limbs, usually called arms. They contain no bones, which helps the animal squeeze through narrow spaces.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7998-b7c9-1f144cbdb911","description":"8","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7944-9f68-5599d69617ea","description":"6","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-71ae-8559-ace9fad870f4","description":"10","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-744b-a2d1-7a7fe1b76bb4","description":"14","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-74af-ab9d-eff743417c29","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"The chemistry of life centers around which element?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Carbon has four valence electrons, allowing it to form stable bonds with many elements and build the chains and rings found in biomolecules.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-72b4-9606-935c5a285c58","description":"Carbon","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7f9b-ac8f-80d7840d985e","description":"Phosphorus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7785-8ebf-ef8161f4309e","description":"Magnesium","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7311-ae98-e5169bd29e41","description":"Lithium","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-77f6-8366-5eb1b679c690","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which scale is used to classify the magnitude of earthquakes?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Charles F. Richter and Beno Gutenberg introduced the scale in 1935. It is logarithmic, so each whole-number increase represents a tenfold increase in measured wave amplitude.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-781e-9a1a-13c439c2c71b","description":"Richter","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7e54-a601-3b5d5bf738f6","description":"Beaufort","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7168-b1bf-b35f62a108b1","description":"Schweizer","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7f86-9338-b4a7829091aa","description":"Hammer","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7549-9cc7-d508921e04ec","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which organism eats only meat?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Carnivores get their food from animals; herbivores eat plants, while omnivores eat both.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-74cb-ab44-23da397096f4","description":"Carnivore","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7560-90c3-e563ae6359fd","description":"Herbivore","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-758b-a290-65f234155ecc","description":"Omnivore","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7ef6-9d05-c233b089fae0","description":"Vegan","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-70bc-bc29-712a50a8b001","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What animal is known as Orcinus orca?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Killer whale is the common name for Orcinus orca. Despite the name, it is the largest dolphin species.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7a49-8270-a4041b7aa254","description":"Killer whale","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-76d6-9e32-95606840fa26","description":"Badger","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-725e-9d6f-11abdfa99b38","description":"Orchard bee","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7c48-810e-0a559b0b0c9b","description":"Camel","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-713f-b4f8-7bae62e4076b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which bird often stands on one leg?","difficul