cription":"Magnetic force","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7f6c-b4d0-c9c08a0497e1","description":"Air resistance","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7470-8a43-36682c23495d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What was created with the big bang?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The Big Bang was the expansion of the early Universe, not an explosion into preexisting empty space.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7afe-a055-fb92448b2ac1","description":"The Universe","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-77d2-9e36-1298016dc861","description":"The Milky Way","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7da7-bc55-f04edc0c849f","description":"Andromeda","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7823-a740-a45669e37d4f","description":"Infinity","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7152-aefb-606d693586e0","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"A female horse is known as what?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A mare is an adult female horse; a young female horse is called a filly.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7c47-b806-10f02c9a61ba","description":"A Mare","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7418-9eab-d09fdd65c361","description":"A Hen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7a26-9afd-b0b9ebe14fa0","description":"A Hembra","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-728e-b9e5-b57c332af499","description":"A Jill","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7902-9072-bbb2af095f0f","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a female dog?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A bitch is also the term for a female wolf or fox.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7965-ba1b-6fb3bc395d2c","description":"A Bitch","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7784-a649-bc97dc6bc53f","description":"A Jill","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7577-8bf2-a8f63de7ffed","description":"A Gander","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-723f-b794-8d19b7515c06","description":"A Tigeress","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7497-a8ec-0be6fb3ad941","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"People with which condition should avoid milk products?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Lactose intolerance involves difficulty digesting lactose, the sugar in milk, which can cause digestive symptoms after consuming dairy.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7add-8d5c-a506e39123e8","description":"Lactose intolerance","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-799a-8054-7731b785d366","description":"Cystic fibrosis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-74b2-9de1-a70839334711","description":"Sickle-cell disease","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-779d-aa0c-7ba31101f47a","description":"Color blindness","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-778a-a6aa-3d2906b742aa","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What type of animal is a caribou?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Reindeer belong to the deer family; unusually, both males and females grow antlers.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-793a-b3a0-58df5da21998","description":"A Reindeer","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7683-b33c-ee7fcd8e0ffb","description":"A Whale","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-77f7-806d-4a6d6423a504","description":"A Mouse","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-73bc-b730-ba6cf3a61035","description":"A Spider","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-794d-b2dc-bacd99c50b00","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Pediatrics is the branch of medicine that provides care for which of these groups?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Infants receive pediatric care, and pediatricians also treat patients through adolescence.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-73c8-83cb-5bbca4e51ccc","description":"Infants","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7b41-863a-9aaa9e822d66","description":"Elders","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-71b0-82e6-9c6bddafd8c7","description":"Veterans","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7084-8a46-7300a71a1fb3","description":"Women","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7db5-93d8-8785a87c1a04","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the death of an entire species?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Extinction is global when no individuals of a species remain anywhere; disappearing from one region alone does not count.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-726b-a117-79dc4c90bf39","description":"Extinction","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7cf3-bd2d-bdbaf5b51fdd","description":"Adaptation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7ae2-a9c3-9df64c92376b","description":"Evolution","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7d75-a1f8-5a85c3724d0f","description":"Migration","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-725f-a640-63d6a93b13fb","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What does pH measure?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A pH of 7 is neutral; lower readings indicate greater acidity, while higher readings indicate greater alkalinity.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7648-a9f7-90a977eb0293","description":"Acidity and alkalinity","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-76ef-8f2c-fd9c6ecb31b1","description":"Temperature","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7856-8f12-d5c027570843","description":"Density","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-70f9-a6c6-a88cea5130df","description":"Electrical conductivity","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-79ce-b441-8c63d538a679","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Where can we find mitochondria?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Mitochondria produce much of the ATP that powers processes in eukaryotic cells.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7976-926b-57408e3e6c26","description":"In cells","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7682-a238-366c88859cb2","description":"In viruses","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-73fa-8c91-f068929a575a","description":"In the nucleus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-72ca-84e9-746b26ac0046","description":"In blood plasma","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7520-aeb5-e51647ddaddb","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is an ion?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"An ion has an unequal number of protons and electrons, giving it a net charge; gaining or losing electrons creates that imbalance.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7dc8-9e79-f04044865b42","description":"An atom or molecule with an electric charge","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7cc3-a371-af0dbace4d1c","description":"An atom with no electric charge","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-74fc-be17-4147ee6394bc","description":"A chemical bond between two atoms","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-72f6-a141-eaca3b8a8040","description":"A particle of light","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7842-8c3c-7b2812eec31e","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Parasitology the study of?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Parasitology examines parasites and their relationships with the organisms they live on or in, called hosts.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7d0a-9cb1-f5dc1fe0768e","description":"parasites","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7cda-ba9a-2dba1dfee039","description":"crime","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-72f2-95ba-3831dac3685e","description":"nutrition","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7c1d-bdee-85ebd2d8aa0b","description":"the signification and application of words","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7daf-9e71-95a24181e449","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What acts as an exchange surface between mother and embryo?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The placenta attaches to the uterine wall, and the umbilical cord carries substances between it and the fetus; their blood supplies generally remain separate.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-70c3-a65b-412ce9afc4fe","description":"Placenta","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7617-a54c-c07702c5a7b8","description":"Ovaries","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7a6a-b656-b319d8244220","description":"Cervix","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7cb3-8f2e-45728aee62c9","description":"Anus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-754e-b387-8be32aa3b39b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What cell component is often used for personal identification?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"DNA carries inherited genetic information, and forensic profiling compares variable regions to help distinguish people.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-733f-8f29-df7d70138b2f","description":"DNA","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-75f8-8d24-e918b7696fec","description":"Golgi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7e16-961a-d729c5e713ec","description":"Membrane","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-751c-9a2d-e35709f07aa3","description":"Cytoplasm","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7811-816f-6da5c890a562","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is a decrease in hemoglobin or the number of red blood cells?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Anemia can cause weakness and shortness of breath because less oxygen reaches the body\'s tissues.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-798c-b948-124602b58778","description":"Anemia","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7834-b56f-23603475727e","description":"Dengue","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7272-860a-0e1f91f26fd2","description":"Scurvy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7577-971f-660c71ac6dad","description":"Hypothermia","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7ff7-93e5-92425e04d9eb","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What paper size measures 210 mm \u00d7 297 mm?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A4 belongs to ISO 216\'s A series, whose sheets keep the same proportions when each size is halved.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7b72-a0d0-40f2b45c14a0","description":"A4","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7bb4-b5b3-0018e619c671","description":"A3","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7263-a980-23630feba58f","description":"A5","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7e0c-973d-9d7fbd5727f5","description":"A2","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-73d5-b437-e64c559c66eb","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What do we call the center of an atom?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The nucleus contains nearly all an atom\u2019s mass, with protons and neutrons held together by the strong nuclear force.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7bda-ba43-4e4fd52c8122","description":"Nucleus","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-73ea-a346-12f97f89d53f","description":"Pivot","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-795e-8380-8473bf5ac533","description":"Epicenter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-734f-8722-76147d68d6a8","description":"Fulcrum","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-72c0-8590-1b48cd9c46fc","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is futurology the study of?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Futurology uses trends across fields such as technology, economics, and society to explore possible scenarios; it does not claim certainty about The Future.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-72b2-a99e-cc4d70b69b7d","description":"The Future","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-72bd-85a4-0cf95a385f0c","description":"Science Fiction","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-70f4-9504-9b658846ca1d","description":"Palm Reading","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-773e-a212-3b30aa87e1cf","description":"Drugs","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7912-8250-f6c73cb1e107","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which organs do most fish use to breathe underwater?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Fish gills extract dissolved oxygen from water passing over them.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7662-ba6d-ac362ae0c3fa","description":"Gills","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7a0f-8f15-993e4ff3c1f6","description":"Lungs","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7de4-84da-225024311e91","description":"Fins","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7b33-924d-f6e653605965","description":"Scales","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-771d-a638-ef9d4cf95ad4","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which condition is NOT genetically caused?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Tetanus is caused by a toxin made by Clostridium tetani bacteria, not by inherited genetic changes. Vaccination can prevent it.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-73ef-a2ce-c365604f51d7","description":"Tetanus","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7a24-b9c4-ed18c731b3c1","description":"Down syndrome","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-76d1-ad71-838baad98fbd","description":"Cystic fibrosis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-76fa-a940-753c0c5182df","description":"Sickle-cell disease","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-78db-81dd-cedf115ec7fb","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of the space telescope that was placed in Earth\'s orbit in 1990?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The Hubble Space Telescope was deployed from the Space Shuttle Discovery. Astronauts later serviced it during several missions.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7e2a-a646-0ac486b5181d","description":"Hubble","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7093-a52e-32475c0e4bcc","description":"Bubble","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7352-963b-b1acd21b6513","description":"Toil","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7e61-b50e-9d78eee07632","description":"Trouble","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-77ad-a81a-b67a30d06291","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the most widely accepted theory for the creation of the universe?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"The Big Bang theory is supported by the cosmic microwave background, cooled radiation left over from the universe\u2019s early hot, dense state.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7ac5-921b-46293500bd49","description":"Big Bang","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7838-b0c4-c98207ba4278","description":"Eternal Inflation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7b66-8f2c-3261e1ae7ac0","description":"Steady State","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7a8b-a71e-57b738536d00","description":"Oscillating Model","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-73d8-bed7-71eb52648ff0","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many horns does a wildebeest have?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Wildebeest have two horns, and both males and females grow them.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7064-b05f-efad65ff4e11","description":"2","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7c56-bd77-5ee7511f4aaa","description":"1","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7579-ba67-5341138c53af","description":"0","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-71ab-98c9-cb3bdb0f4806","description":"4","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-79a8-aea5-e799f8de4e97","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which of these is an antiseptic?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Ethano