312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many eyes does a king cobra have?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A king cobra has two eyes, one on each side of its head; a clear scale called a spectacle covers each eye.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7139-872a-6c38b4908834","description":"2","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-71d8-995f-b759075cd8b5","description":"8","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7126-a0c6-47ec1ac6ead7","description":"None","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7a66-b9fc-5f2c5660a8ba","description":"4","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7a0a-9faf-6112b5b2c988","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which nuclear process occurs inside an atomic bomb?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Fission releases energy when heavy atomic nuclei break into lighter ones, producing neutrons that can trigger further reactions in a rapidly growing chain.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7385-8ec7-bc7696dad9bd","description":"Fission","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7864-a426-2306af9cdb7a","description":"Fusion","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-726b-9fa1-55c8b287e0d5","description":"Combustion","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7b85-98fb-e22c08f9321a","description":"Radioactive decay","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-74bd-b669-db5d94e0e9f0","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What instrument do doctors often have around their necks?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"A stethoscope carries sounds from the body to the listener\'s ears; its name comes from Greek roots meaning chest and examine.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7872-a06f-c289869b68e0","description":"Stethoscope","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7361-8345-476084a9edba","description":"MRI Scanner","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-73e4-93ac-616fe1b2e4a4","description":"Forceps","correct_answer":false},{"