,"difficulty":1,"explanation":"Isaac Newton also built an early practical reflecting telescope, which used mirrors rather than lenses to form an image.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7261-b268-44e7abd2e47a","description":"Isaac","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-71a8-b438-cef161ae8b76","description":"Albert","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-76ea-8b76-894c854bf23d","description":"Herbert","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7db5-b7ad-d4dbc8acc732","description":"Luigi","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7341-b415-8a189089fe65","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of the red gem that symbolizes health and wisdom, and is the birthstone for July?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Rubies and sapphires are both forms of corundum; trace amounts of chromium give rubies their red color.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7e34-bed5-95e8149495aa","description":"Ruby","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-71b6-ae94-2c1938601db0","description":"Emerald","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7726-a2c6-73cf07bba6c3","description":"Sapphire","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-73cf-a3ca-9b30a76e3cfd","description":"Diamond","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-74e8-b045-cc169eebe564","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of the salty, watery fluid secreted by sweat glands?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Perspiration is produced mainly by eccrine glands, and its evaporation helps cool the body.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5547-77c9-a250-d3b09739156e","description":"Perspiration","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7cb3-888a-4a0ceaa40908","description":"Saline","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-79ca-a94c-43db9d00f067","description":"Lactate","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5547-7cbd-83f8-8d74c2bc3d90","description":"Water","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"0