elped establish the field.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5548-7c2f-b04f-87bb2c5857aa","description":"Genetics","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5548-7a96-957b-5fc3ed5430f2","description":"Paleontology","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5548-7c30-b83a-6a9065f58552","description":"Macrobiology","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5548-74c2-8331-7d2819571362","description":"Zoology","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5548-7d11-9365-9a1aca122085","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is a skin specialist called?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Dermatologists also treat disorders of hair and nails, which are closely related to skin.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5548-76c2-9700-9bb537aebc42","description":"Dermatologist","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5548-7bc5-a778-6d2cea8166d7","description":"Permologist","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5548-77b7-b3fa-dd7e5c308fe8","description":"Skin Clinician","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5548-7a90-819a-690c46bbb416","description":"Visologist","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5548-72b2-a388-2e496ffa04a8","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many kidneys do humans have?","difficulty":1,"explanation":"Humans typically have two kidneys, one on each side of the spine; many people can live with just one functioning kidney.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-5548-7556-bfaf-37062b1caf1f","description":"2","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-5548-7104-bfa5-a1c32c74c186","description":"1","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5548-7425-9dcd-f75389d6188f","description":"4","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-5548-7e02-b88c-90615b2b22a1","description":"8","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-5548-7eb6-b727-1e10325cd3d5","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How long does it take for Earth to rotate around its axis?","difficulty":1,"explanat